## What is the ECR Club?

The ECR Club is an online forum to give Early Career Researchers (ECRs), i.e., PhD students and junior PostDocs (until 4 years after PhD) who are members of the ECREA Political Communication Section and/or the ECPR’s Standing Group on Political Communication to present and discuss their research related to political communication, broadly perceived. The idea is to create an (online) safe space in which we can bring ECRs from different institutions together (= **networking**), help them to understand and navigate the (often unwritten) rules of academia (= **socialising**) and, of course, help them develop their research (= **feedback on research**) by receiving detailed constructive feedback from peers and senior researchers.
The ECR Club was founded in 2025 by myself and Alena Kluknavská (Masaryk University, Brno). Curious about the session we already had? Then check the [ECPR page](https://ecpr.eu/events/332).  


## Roles

In order to tackle the above-formulated goals (networking, socialising, feedback), we define 2 main roles for each session. (1) The presenter will be the ECR themselves; (2) a discussant will be another researcher (ECR or more senior) who is appointed beforehand for providing detailed, constructive feedback. The ECR is welcome to propose and contact possible discussants, but the organising team will be mainly responsible for recruiting discussants from their own network. In addition to these roles, (3) one member of the organising team will serve as chair of each session and lead the Q&A.


